#901
"Garnie Lane"
"Garnie Lane runs from north to south here, ending to the north at the grey

stone of the town gates and to the south the green of the Village Square.  A

sturdy building of stone rests imposingly to the west, with steps leading up

to the door and the yard before it planted neatly with flowers.  @e'Bank of

Chiiron'@n the sign swinging quietly from a wrought iron post reads, revealing

the reason for the thick, granite walls.  A round tower of the same stone

rises to the east, though no plants grow in the neatly kept yard around it.

"
