#903
"Village Square"
"This is the center of the village of Chiiron, known to residents as the

Village Square.  In the center of the crossroads, a pale grey fountain can be

seen, with fresh, flowing water for the use of the town.  To the side of the

fountain is a small @esign@n, crafted of brass and mounted upon a stone marker.

The Trader Road crosses east to west here, with Garnie Lane leading north from

this junction.

"
