#912
"The Fighting Ferret"
"Every town needs a place for the residents to unwind after a long day at work,

and Chiiron is no exception.  Well kept and clean, like the rest of the town,

the polished wood of the floor and furnishings shows evidence of the town's

skilled woodworkers.  The bar is footed by a shiny brass footrail, and there

are several trophy heads of beasts, probably caught by the townsfolk, hanging

upon the walls of the warm, well-lit room.

"
"[Godwin] Why do only bards know how to play the piano?

