#913
"Grummeltupper's Gadgets"
"The soft and diluted glow of candlelight reflects against the quartered

windows, illuminating the shop with the help of the crackling fire burning in

the hearth.  Long oak tables divide the quaint shop and shelves line the

walls, cluttered with oddities of various sizes and shapes.  A series of

pipes, levers and small chains runs haphazardly along the wood-beam ceiling,

congregating at the wall beside the front door.  A shining flower of radiant

purple sways lazily in the mild breeze, flowing gently from the open funnel,

descending from a web of dull copper above.  Along the southern wall, an

antique wooden desk and countertop draw the attention of the room, a large oil

lamp glowing softly even in the day, casting a yellow hue to the bundles of

scrolls and parchments that rest atop it.  To one side, a small workbench

holds a few metal tools and a thin film of sawdust.

"
