"desk scrolls lamp oil parchment"
"This large oak desk provides the counter necessary for all good shops, though

it's quite evident the space is used as much for thought and design as for the

transfer of money.  Large scrolls of various colors sit in piles, some bound

with string, others lying open to reveal exquisite sketches of models that

elude the common understanding.  A large oil lamp hangs from a peg behind the

counter, casting a blanket of warm, yellow light upon the entire area.  Among

the scattered papers, tools, and tiny items of display, two books show

evidence of recent use.  One, a simple, string-bound journal, contains some of

the recent contracts, creations and transactions of the shop's owner...though

the writing is almost indecipherable.  The other, a hard bound volume with a

sizable number of pages, is titled: \"Politics, the Mechanical Nature of

Society.\" Atop the desk sits a small, black box, and on it...a button.  A

small note pinned to the wood reads: \"@eRing Me@n.\"

"
E
"pipes lever chains ceiling wall"
"Behind the front door, spread upon the wall like metal vines, is a contraption

of intricate beauty.  A gleaming cube with small, depressible buttons rests

upon a cylindrical axle, a host of complimentary and inverted levers

interpreting the press of a key, and reacting with dozens of movements.  To

the side, further down the axle, a similar host awaits silently, with a series

of weighted bars to guide the intended shift's descent.  A few of the levers

and gears extend to a small box above the door, and disappear into the frame. 

There seems to be some sort of code within the design of this creation, but it

remains buried far within the mesh structure.

