"Temple of Taranth"
"The Temple of Taranth is an open, airy building, constructed sturdily of basic

materials.  The interior walls are whitewashed and clean, and hangings of

simple linen serve as curtains on windows and for privacy for those needing

healing.  Poised at the center point of the south wall, a white statue of

Taranth stands, flowers at her base and crowning her.  At the southwest corner

of the room is a small spiral staircase, crafted entirely of wood, granting

access to the belfry.  In the northwest corner of the room, a @ecauldron@n rests

above a small hearth, providing sustenance for those in need.

